<%# THE PROJECTS LIST'S EMPTY STATE — one definition, rendered by BOTH views
    (the table and the cards), so the two can never disagree about why nothing
    is shown. The issue's honest state (#10): "no records match. clear the
    filters." plus the reset link, because a page that says only "nothing here"
    leaves the operator to work out whether the workspace is empty or the
    search is.

    A query that matched nothing is not the same state as a workspace that has
    never had a project: the first is a search with no hits, the second is a
    workspace to fill. The missing-record page's "Search for <stem>" link lands
    on the first (#4), so a blank card would read as the link having done
    nothing. The term is NAMED, then the reset link is offered. %>
<div class="card empty-state">
  <% if @query.present? %>
    <p>no records match. clear the filters.</p>
    <p class="empty-state-reset">
      no project is named <span class="mono"><%= @query %></span> &mdash;
      <%= link_to "Show every project", projects_path, class: "query-clear" %>
    </p>
  <% else %>
    <p>No projects yet. Create one to start running jobs and building composites.</p>
  <% end %>
</div>
